    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling Saturday, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.95). **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play today; facing the hittable Nick Martinez, he benefits from a potent combination of a +16% park factor and a +17% SP skill advantage. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is in a prime spot against Carlos Rod\u00f3n, where a +7% platoon edge and a favorable slot in the two-hole make him a core offensive driver. While **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) is our primary source of speed today\u2014bolstered by a slow opposing delivery that increases his stolen base equity\u2014his matchup against Joe Ober remains the high-water mark for our outfield production.\n\nThe decision to start **Coby Mayo** (62.44) over potential alternatives reflects the optimizer\u2019s preference for raw power against a struggling Nick Martinez. **Coby Mayo** earns his spot through a +16% park boost, successfully offsetting a minor negative platoon swing. Meanwhile, **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Sam Antonacci** (55.29) occupy the lower tier of our active roster. **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s placement at lead-off is a strategic play for R, leveraging his position against a softer pitcher, while **Miguel Vargas** (47.33) remains a marginal play that barely survived the cut; his sub-50 score was dragged down by an unfavorable matchup against McLean, despite a wind-assisted park factor. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of our sidelined core, with **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** all confirmed as unavailable due to IL stints. **Heliot Ramos** was the closest to challenging our current configuration, but his absence from the official lineup confirmed our decision to keep him on the bench. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Kyle Tucker** (58.86); while he remains a focal point of our offensive strategy, his moderate score against a tougher-than-average pitching profile suggests he is a candidate for underperformance today if the weather conditions shift.",
